@@ -0,0 +1,68 @@
+# LAST 64K then near1M source packet — not dispatched
+
+This is a single-use, serial two-request Linux systemd client of the existing ordinary production
+MiMo owner. It neither launches nor adopts a model. No GO or result is supplied.
+Only root may approve deployment after FINAL native 17-tool, actual ordinary
+production, and Sova acceptance all PASS. W2 must pause Sova again and hold the
+shared frontier exclusively for the entire job, with all other three models
+loaded idle. A previous Sova PASS does not establish this later exclusive lane.
+
+Stage under `/data/build/H016-20260927/worker1-final13-long`; precreate the private
+registered log directory `/data/logs/H016-20260927/worker1-final13-long` with the
+installed anchored guards. Install/start the supplied unit only after exact-source
+review and GO. There is no dispatch script. Existing source and owner protections
+apply. The service has no dependency that starts or stop-orders the production owner.
+Its preflight and live guard require the already-running exact owner. It has
+`Restart=no`, an 8-hour active cap and a 65-second stop
+allowance; root must choose a finite hard-end epoch and an admission deadline at
+least eight hours earlier. Neither bound is the foreground 17:48 window.
+
+`ROOT-GO.json` is a protected root-owned authority input, not a new production
+manifest. Required fields are documented directly by `validate_go` and
+`preflight`. Bind the exact client, existing ordinary owner, and complete reader
+import closure in `source_sha256`; `reader_directory` selects the reviewed R9
+reader source. Bind current production manifest digest and exact state keys
+`boot_id`, `manifest_sha256`, `supervisor`, `launch_id`, `native` in
+`production_identity`. Each `acceptance` entry names an actual existing protected
+JSON receipt by `path`, `sha256`, `status_field`, and `expected_value` (`PASS` or
+`PASSED`). Root reviews the content and binds it to this exact qualification and
+production configuration; this wrapper verifies the unchanged source/receipt
+bytes, not arbitrary semantic equivalence across receipt formats. Root GO must
+also attest `w2_exclusive_frontier_sova_paused`, `other_three_loaded_idle`, and
+`lane_exclusive_until_epoch`. W2 owns and enforces that remote application lane;
+this ai-vm client cannot independently inspect the frontend host.
+
+Both requests use the production private IPv4 API at `10.156.100.60:30012`, the
+exact reviewed owner/model/template/source pins, actual authenticated slot, and
+existing production guard receipts. No direct-loopback inference bypass. The
+existing owner continues enforcing GPU free >=7%, host free >=15%, no owned swap,
+and the 85C/lower cutoff; five-second receipt consumption fails closed if owner
+identity or fresh guard proof disappears. No new hardware monitor is introduced.
+
+Actual usable slots 1,000,000 and 1,000,192 are accepted independently from any
+physical pool. The first request uses exact input 65,536/output 256/thinking false and the same bounded retrieval/arithmetic fixture. Only its semantic, DONE, full-drain and idle PASS permits the near-limit request. Distinct durable receipts retain the 64K result even if the second request cannot fit. Status is 64K running/near1M queued until the latter actually begins. Exact near-limit inputs are respectively 998,975 and 999,167,
+leaving 1,024 output tokens and one native slot. The native input-count route is
+used on the final payload before submission; each count socket timeout is capped at 15 seconds and measured count elapsed above 15 seconds refuses dispatch; no equality is fabricated and no
+reload corrects rounding. A reviewed 917,504 fallback is not silently accepted by
+this LAST source: it would require an explicit source/root review amendment.
+
+The reviewed R9 fixture and reader provide genuine varied technical retrieval,
+exact token counting, private raw monotonic chunks, first/last output, usage,
+DONE, native timings, full HTTP drain, and authenticated idle-slot settlement.
+The wrapper adds durable BODY-SENT and guard-progress receipts; request bodies and
+raw traces remain private registered files and never console/Git logs. There is
+no per-token guard, fsync, lifecycle lease, or receipt rewrite. Default verbosity
+remains the server's configured 3; no unsupported request field is introduced.
+
+One shared eight-hour absolute client deadline covers both requests; admission forecasts never shorten it. On both PASS the production model remains warm and selection unchanged. Any possibly
+active failed/interrupted request triggers this unit's `ExecStopPost`: it verifies
+all source pins and the pinned production invocation and calls only the existing production unit's
+ordinary stop/settlement. Ambiguous request hold remains preserved. There is no
+automatic retry, restart, GLM selection, or rollback; subsequent recovery stays
+with the existing reviewed owner and root. If the owner identity changed, this
+client refuses to touch the replacement and reports failure. SIGKILL recovery is
+owned by systemd, not a foreground CLI child.
+
+Verification: 9 focused local tests PASS; import and Python syntax PASS. No Linux
+unit/runtime execution, live API, long request, or production acceptance was
+performed. The client remains SOURCE ONLY.
